{
  "tema": 7176,
  "slug": "llevar-gerundio",
  "titulo": "Using llevar + gerund to express how long an action has been going on",
  "subtitulo": "Llevo tres años surfeando: how long, so far.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "Llevar (present or imperfect) + time + gerund = have / had been doing for: llevo tres días estudiando. Negative: llevar + time + sin + infinitive.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say how long an action **has been going on**, use **llevar** (conjugated) + the **gerund**, with the length of time."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**llevar**",
            "time",
            "gerund"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The time can go between **llevar** and the gerund, or at the end: **llevo tres días estudiando** = **llevo estudiando tres días**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Only the **present** (**llevo**) and the **imperfect** (**llevaba**) are used with this structure, never the perfect tenses. English uses _have been doing / had been doing_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Negative**: **llevar** + time + **sin** + **infinitive** (after a preposition, always an infinitive): **llevo un mes sin fumar** = _I haven't smoked for a month_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **llevo** is like carrying the time on your back: **llevo tres años surfeando**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Beto ==lleva== dos años ==trabajando== en esa escuela.",
              "en": "Beto has been working at that school for two years."
            },
            {
              "es": "El profe ==llevaba== diez minutos ==hablando== con el alumno cuando entramos.",
              "en": "The teacher had been talking to the student for ten minutes when we came in."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Llevo== tres días ==estudiando== para el examen.",
              "en": "I've been studying for the exam for three days."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Llevamos== una hora ==esperando== el camión.",
              "en": "We've been waiting for the bus for an hour."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Llevo== un mes ==sin fumar==.",
              "en": "I haven't smoked for a month."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Llevaba== una semana ==sin surfear== y ya extrañaba el mar.",
              "en": "I hadn't surfed for a week and I already missed the sea."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
